-- title:
--   The real-valued indicator of a set
-- statement:
--   The **indicator function of a set, valued in $\mathbb{R}$**: $\mathbf 1_S(x)$ is $1$ when
--   $x \in S$ and $0$ otherwise.
--
--   Section 3 of Bux–Kassmann–Schulze writes $\mathbf 1_{V^\Gamma[x]}(y)$ throughout — in
--   assumption (2), in Lemma 3.2's inequality, and in the two-sided bounds of Proposition 3.5
--   and Corollary 3.6 — for the quantity that is $1$ exactly when $y$ lies in the cone based at
--   $x$. This is that function, in the real-valued form Lemma 3.2 is stated with. The
--   $[0,\infty]$-valued companion used once the estimates move into `ℝ≥0∞` is `QFS.indE`.
